>. The video must begin exactly on <Picture 1> and end exactly on <Picture 2>, conveying the quiet passage of time from morning to afternoon through subtle changes in light, coffee level, and the appearance of a book and reading glasses.\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description: A quiet still-life time study, shot on 35mm film with warm natural lighting, shallow depth of field, soft film grain, and a gentle shift in light direction from left (morning) to right (afternoon). The video opens on <Picture 1>: a white ceramic cup filled with dark black coffee, thick steam rising, on a warm wooden tabletop, soft morning light from the left.\n\n[Shot 1] The camera holds in a static close-up as steam continues to rise from the hot coffee in curling wisps, the morning light from the left slowly shifting angle and warming in tone, a shadow from the cup gradually moving across the wooden table surface, the coffee level beginning to lower imperceptibly as if being sipped over time.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:04.000, the camera cuts to the same close-up angle, now with afternoon light coming from the right, as a hand enters frame briefly and places an open hardcover book and a pair of tortoiseshell reading glasses next to the now-empty white ceramic cup with a faint coffee stain at the bottom, then the hand exits frame, leaving the still life settled in warm afternoon light, ending exactly on <Picture 2>.\n\noverall_soundscape: The faint hiss of rising steam, a quiet ambient room tone, the soft sound of pages being turned in the distance, the gentle clink of a cup being set down, and the subtle shift from morning bird sounds to quiet afternoon stillness.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: A sparse, warm acoustic guitar piece with slow fingerpicked notes and generous sustain, gentle and unhurried, conveying the quiet comfort of a slow morning turning into a relaxed afternoon, fading softly at the end.\n", 1344, 768, 73], "inputs": [{"name": "clip", "link": 33, "label": "clip", "type": "CLIP", "localized_n